---
import Layout from '../../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../../styles/ai.css';
---

<Layout
  title="Llama 4 — Meta — A.I. — Rycode"
  description="Meta’s current open-weight generation: Llama 4 Scout and Llama 4 Maverick."
  variant="ai"
>
  <article class="ai-model">
    <p class="ai-model-kicker">Meta · Llama</p>
    <h1 class="ai-model-title">Llama 4</h1>
    <p class="ai-model-dek">Llama 4 is Meta’s current open-weight generation. Public cards center on Llama 4 Scout and Llama 4 Maverick (Mixture-of-Experts style naming on Meta and GitHub herd tables). Meta’s Llama 4 developer page frames them as optimized for deployment and efficiency.</p>
    <hr class="ai-model-rule" />
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Training</h2>
    <p>Parameter and expert layouts on Meta and GitHub herd notes include Scout-17B-16E and Maverick-17B-128E. Full FLOPs and data mix are not published unless a Meta model card states them. License is the Llama community license (not Apache). Read exact license text from Meta’s page.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Inference</h2>
    <p>Open weights via Meta Llama download flow and Hugging Face <code>meta-llama</code> repos. Multimodal image reasoning scores appear on Meta’s Llama 4 page. Serving silicon for end users is the buyer’s hardware or cloud.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Context</h2>
    <p>GitHub <code>llama-models</code> README associates Scout with very long context (10M note) and Maverick with 1M. Confirm on live Meta model cards before treating those figures as final.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Methods</h2>
    <p>Open-weight Llama post-training stack. Exact RL recipe for Scout and Maverick is not published unless a model card says so.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Benchmarking</h2>
    <p>Use only scores printed on the Llama 4 developer page or official model cards. Examples Meta lists there include MMMU, MathVista, ChartQA, DocVQA, and others.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Hardware</h2>
    <p>Meta has not published per-SKU training silicon for Llama 4 on the pages cited here. Buyers run weights on their own GPUs or hosts.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Sources</h2>
    <ul class="ai-model-sources">
      <li><a href="https://developer.meta.com/ai/models/llama-4/">Llama 4 developer page</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/meta-llama/llama-models/">meta-llama/llama-models</a></li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</Layout>
